('SS1', 'science', 'Biology', 'Cell structure', 'Which cell structure selectively controls substances entering and leaving a cell?', 'Ribosome', 'Cell membrane', 'Nucleolus', 'Vacuole', 'B', 'The cell membrane is selectively permeable and regulates exchange with the surroundings.', 'easy', '1', 'true'),
('SS1', 'science', 'Biology', 'Cell organisation', 'Which sequence shows levels of organisation from simplest to most complex?', 'Organ → cell → tissue → system', 'Tissue → cell → system → organ', 'Cell → tissue → organ → system', 'Cell → organ → tissue → system', 'C', 'Similar cells form tissues; tissues form organs, and organs work together in systems.', 'easy', '1', 'true'),
('SS1', 'science', 'Biology', 'Nutrition in plants', 'During photosynthesis, which raw material supplies the carbon atoms used to form glucose?', 'Oxygen from the air', 'Nitrogen from the soil', 'Chlorophyll from the leaf', 'Carbon dioxide from the air', 'D', 'Carbon dioxide provides the carbon that is incorporated into carbohydrate during photosynthesis.', 'medium', '1', 'true'),
('SS1', 'science', 'Biology', 'Transport in plants', 'Which plant tissue transports manufactured sugars from leaves to other parts?', 'Phloem', 'Xylem', 'Epidermis', 'Cambium only', 'A', 'Phloem translocates sugars and other organic substances through the plant.', 'easy', '1', 'true'),
('SS1', 'science', 'Biology', 'Cell respiration', 'In which organelle does most aerobic respiration in a eukaryotic cell take place?', 'Chloroplast', 'Mitochondrion', 'Golgi apparatus', 'Vacuole', 'B', 'Mitochondria are the main sites of aerobic respiration and ATP production in eukaryotic cells.', 'medium', '1', 'true'),

('SS1', 'science', 'Chemistry', 'Atomic structure', 'An atom has atomic number 11 and mass number 23. How many neutrons are in its nucleus?', '12', '11', '23', '34', 'A', 'Neutrons = mass number − atomic number = 23 − 11 = 12.', 'easy', '1', 'true'),
